<title>EGYPT: Egypt mulls buying Bombardier CRJ planes.</title>
<headline>Egypt mulls buying Bombardier CRJ planes.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Egyptian national carrier EgyptAir is thinking of buying two 50-seat Canadair Regional Jets (CRJ) for $20 million each from Canada's Bombardier Inc, airline officials said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;They are still in negotiations,&quot;an EgyptAir official said.</p>
<p>EgyptAir chairman Mohamed Fahim Rayan last week made a trial trip to the Red Sea resort of Hurghada on board a CRJ, airport sources said.</p>
<p>The officials said EgyptAir would use the two planes to carry people to a recently launched irrigation scheme in Toshka, some 700 km(435 miles) south of Cairo.</p>
</text>
